nic prediction from multiple computational programs (PhyloP: C; SIFT: D; PolyPhen-2: D; Likelihood Ratio Test (LRT): D; MutationTaster: N; GERP: D)", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21817", "infons": {"identifier": "472", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "30952", "valid": true, "normalized": [472], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 472, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ATM", "accession": "@GENE_ATM"}, "text": "ATM", "locations": [{"offset": 12417, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "21818", "infons": {"identifier": "tmVar:c|SUB|T|7271|G;HGVS:c.7271T>G;VariantGroup:0;CorrespondingGene:472;RS#:28904921;CorrespondingSpecies:9606;CA#:115930", "type": "Variant", "valid": true, "subtype": "DNAMutation", "database": "litvar", "hgvs": "c.7271T>G", "gene_ids": [472], "gene_id": 472, "rsids": ["rs28904921"], "species_ids": [9606], "species_id": 9606, "clingen_id": "CA115930", "rsid": "rs28904921", "normalized": ["rs28904921##", "#472#", "CA115930#rs28904921##"], "normalized_id": "rs28904921##", "biotype": "variant", "name": "c.7271T>G", "accession": "@VARIANT_c.7271T>G_ATM_human"}, "text": "c.7271 T > G", "locations": [{"offset": 12433, "length": 12}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "TABLE", "file": "Tab1.xml", "id": "Tab1", "type": "table_foot"}, "offset": 12608, "text": "PhyloP: Conserved (C) or not conserved (N); SIFT: Deleterious (D) or tolerated (T); PolyPhen-2: Damaging (D), possibly damaging (P), or benign (B); Likelihood Ratio Test (LRT): Deleterious (D) or neutral (N); MutationTaster: Deleterious (D) or neutral (N); GERP: Deleterious (D) or neutral (N)", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 12902, "text": "All 9 variants classified via ACMG guidelines as likely pathogenic or pathogenic appeared in LLFS at similar frequencies to general population frequencies (Table 1). These variants were present in both autosomal dominant (BRCA1 and SDHC) and autosomal recessive (CPT2, ACADM, SUMF1, WRN, ATM, and ACADVL) genes (Table 1). ", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21819", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 13124, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21820", "infons": {"identifier": "6391", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2256", "valid": true, "normalized": [6391], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6391, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SDHC", "accession": "@GENE_SDHC"}, "text": "SDHC", "locations": [{"offset": 13134, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21821", "infons": {"identifier": "1376", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "77", "valid": true, "normalized": [1376], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1376, "biotype": "gene", "name": "CPT2", "accession": "@GENE_CPT2"}, "text": "CPT2", "locations": [{"offset": 13165, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21822", "infons": {"identifier": "34", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "3", "valid": true, "normalized": [34], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 34, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ACADM", "accession": "@GENE_ACADM"}, "text": "ACADM", "locations": [{"offset": 13171, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21823", "infons": {"identifier": "285362", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "16268", "valid": true, "normalized": [285362], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 285362, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SUMF1", "accession": "@GENE_SUMF1"}, "text": "SUMF1", "locations": [{"offset": 13178, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21824", "infons": {"identifier": "7486", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "6659", "valid": true, "normalized": [7486], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 7486, "biotype": "gene", "name": "WRN", "accession": "@GENE_WRN"}, "text": "WRN", "locations": [{"offset": 13185, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "21825", "infons": {"identifier": "472", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "30952", "valid": true, "normalized": [472], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 472, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ATM", "accession": "@GENE_ATM"}, "text": "ATM", "locations": [{"offset": 13190, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "21826", "infons": {"identifier": "37", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5", "valid": true, "normalized": [37], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 37, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ACADVL", "accession": "@GENE_ACADVL"}, "text": "ACADVL", "locations": [{"offset": 13199, "length": 6}]}, {"id": "21827", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 12995, "length": 4}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 13225, "text": "Among LLFS participants, the pathogenic BRCA1 variant (NM_007294.3:c.3748G > T) had an allele frequency similar to the general population (0.03% vs. 0.0008%; p = 1) (Table 1). However, the individuals (all heterozygotes), two members of one family (92 year old father and his 49 year old daughter) and one a member of another family (51 year old woman), with this variant present have not been diagnosed with breast, ovarian or prostate cancer. The parental samples of the 92 year old father were not available for evaluation of BRCA1 mutation status. In the second family, the mother of the 51 year old woman did not carry the BRCA1 variant. Though the father's DNA sample was not available for evaluation, we presume this mutation was paternally transmitted though a de novo origin of this mutation cannot be excluded. 18 submissions to ClinVar, ranging from 1994 to 2017 in 657 different individuals from 75 families of varying ethnicities were recorded to have this pathogenic variant in ClinVar in patients with breast or ovarian cancer. Though breast and ovarian cancer due to BRCA1 mutations have a peak incidence in the fourth decade of life, cumulative incidence of these cancers increases till 80 years of age.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21828", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 13265, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21829", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 13754, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21830", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 13853, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21831", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 14308, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21832", "infons": {"type": "Species", "valid": false, "normalized_id": null, "biotype": "species"}, "text": "NM_007294.3", "locations": [{"offset": 13280, "length": 11}]}, {"id": "21833", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D061325", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D061325"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D061325", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Hereditary_Breast_and_Ovarian_Cancer_Syndrome"}, "text": "breast or ovarian cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 14242, "length": 24}]}, {"id": "21834", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 14228, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "21835", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "woman", "locations": [{"offset": 13571, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21836", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "cancers", "locations": [{"offset": 14406, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "21837", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D061325", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D061325"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D061325", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Hereditary_Breast_and_Ovarian_Cancer_Syndrome"}, "text": "breast and ovarian cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 14275, "length": 25}]}, {"id": "21838", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "woman", "locations": [{"offset": 13829, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21839", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 13231, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21840", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010051", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010051"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010051", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Ovarian Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Ovarian_Neoplasms"}, "text": "breast, ovarian or prostate cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 13634, "length": 34}]}, {"id": "21841", "infons": {"identifier": "tmVar:c|SUB|G|3748|T;HGVS:c.3748G>T;VariantGroup:5;CorrespondingGene:672;RS#:28897686;CorrespondingSpecies:9606;CA#:2402", "type": "Variant", "valid": true, "subtype": "DNAMutation", "database": "litvar", "hgvs": "c.3748G>T", "gene_ids": [672], "gene_id": 672, "rsids": ["rs28897686"], "species_ids": [9606], "species_id": 9606, "clingen_id": "CA2402", "rsid": "rs28897686", "normalized": ["rs28897686##", "#672#", "CA2402#rs28897686##"], "normalized_id": "rs28897686##", "biotype": "variant", "name": "c.3748G>T", "accession": "@VARIANT_p.E1250X_BRCA1_human"}, "text": "c.3748G > T", "locations": [{"offset": 13292, "length": 11}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 14468, "text": "The prevalence of the SDHC variant (NM_003001.3:c.397C > T) in LLFS was marginally higher compared to the general population (0.08% vs. 0.003%; p = 0.05) (Table 1). SDHC variants are associated with autosomal dominant inherited paraganglioma and gastric stromal sarcoma. The participants from a single family (all heterozygotes) that included a 99 year old mother, her 63 year old daughter and her 55 year old son, were asymptomatic, to the best of our knowledge. Parental samples of the mother were not available for further evaluation. Six submissions to ClinVar, ranging from 2016 to 2017 have listed this particular variant as pathogenic. Among the evidence submitted to ClinVar, this mutation was present in multiple individuals in different families exhibiting paragangliomas. Since hereditary paragangliomas typically present before 45 years of age, the LLFS participants are older than the typical age of onset for hereditary paragangliomas.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21842", "infons": {"identifier": "6391", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2256", "valid": true, "normalized": [6391], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6391, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SDHC", "accession": "@GENE_SDHC"}, "text": "SDHC", "locations": [{"offset": 14490, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21843", "infons": {"identifier": "6391", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2256", "valid": true, "normalized": [6391], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6391, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SDHC", "accession": "@GENE_SDHC"}, "text": "SDHC", "locations": [{"offset": 14633, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21844", "infons": {"identifier": "tmVar:c|SUB|C|397|T;HGVS:c.397C>T;VariantGroup:1;CorrespondingGene:6391;RS#:764575966;CorrespondingSpecies:9606;CA#:11426", "type": "Variant", "valid": true, "subtype": "DNAMutation", "database": "litvar", "hgvs": "c.397C>T", "gene_ids": [6391], "gene_id": 6391, "rsids": ["rs764575966"], "species_ids": [9606], "species_id": 9606, "clingen_id": "CA11426", "rsid": "rs764575966", "normalized": ["rs764575966##", "#6391#", "CA11426#rs764575966##"], "normalized_id": "rs764575966##", "biotype": "variant", "name": "c.397C>T", "accession": "@VARIANT_c.397C>T_SDHC_human"}, "text": "c.397C > T", "locations": [{"offset": 14516, "length": 10}]}, {"id": "21845", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010235", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010235"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010235", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Paraganglioma", "accession": "@DISEASE_Paraganglioma"}, "text": "paragangliomas", "locations": [{"offset": 15235, "length": 14}]}, {"id": "21846", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009386", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009386"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009386", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplastic Syndromes Hereditary", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplastic_Syndromes_Hereditary"}, "text": "hereditary paragangliomas", "locations": [{"offset": 15391, "length": 25}]}, {"id": "21847", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009386", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009386"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009386", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplastic Syndromes Hereditary", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplastic_Syndromes_Hereditary"}, "text": "hereditary paragangliomas", "locations": [{"offset": 15257, "length": 25}]}, {"id": "21848", "infons": {"type": "Species", "valid": false, "normalized_id": null, "biotype": "species"}, "text": "NM_003001.3", "locations": [{"offset": 14504, "length": 11}]}, {"id": "21849", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 14531, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21850", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C565335", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C565335"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C565335", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Paragangliomas 3", "accession": "@DISEASE_Paragangliomas_3"}, "text": "autosomal dominant inherited paraganglioma", "locations": [{"offset": 14667, "length": 42}]}, {"id": "21851", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C564650", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C564650"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C564650", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carney-Stratakis Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carney_Stratakis_Syndrome"}, "text": "gastric stromal sarcoma", "locations": [{"offset": 14714, "length": 23}]}, {"id": "21852", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 15329, "length": 4}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 15434, "text": "The remaining 7 pathogenic/likely pathogenic variants represented variants in genes that caused autosomal recessive disorders and represented carrier status for these autosomal recessive disorders. As expected, these variants were present in frequencies comparable to the general population. These included variants in CPT2 (n = 1), ACADVL (n = 1), SUMF1 (n = 1), WRN (n = 1), ATM (n = 1) and ACADM (n = 2). Three LLFS participants were homozygous for the pathogenic variant in CPT2 (rs74315294) (Table 1).", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21853", "infons": {"identifier": "1376", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "77", "valid": true, "normalized": [1376], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1376, "biotype": "gene", "name": "CPT2", "accession": "@GENE_CPT2"}, "text": "CPT2", "locations": [{"offset": 15753, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21854", "infons": {"identifier": "37", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5", "valid": true, "normalized": [37], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 37, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ACADVL", "accession": "@GENE_ACADVL"}, "text": "ACADVL", "locations": [{"offset": 15767, "length": 6}]}, {"id": "21855", "infons": {"identifier": "285362", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "16268", "valid": true, "normalized": [285362], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 285362, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SUMF1", "accession": "@GENE_SUMF1"}, "text": "SUMF1", "locations": [{"offset": 15783, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21856", "infons": {"identifier": "7486", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "6659", "valid": true, "normalized": [7486], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 7486, "biotype": "gene", "name": "WRN", "accession": "@GENE_WRN"}, "text": "WRN", "locations": [{"offset": 15798, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "21857", "infons": {"identifier": "472", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "30952", "valid": true, "normalized": [472], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 472, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ATM", "accession": "@GENE_ATM"}, "text": "ATM", "locations": [{"offset": 15811, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "21858", "infons": {"identifier": "34", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "3", "valid": true, "normalized": [34], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 34, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ACADM", "accession": "@GENE_ACADM"}, "text": "ACADM", "locations": [{"offset": 15827, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21859", "infons": {"identifier": "1376", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "77", "valid": true, "normalized": [1376], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1376, "biotype": "gene", "name": "CPT2", "accession": "@GENE_CPT2"}, "text": "CPT2", "locations": [{"offset": 15912, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21860", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D030342", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D030342"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D030342", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Genetic Diseases Inborn", "accession": "@DISEASE_Genetic_Diseases_Inborn"}, "text": "autosomal recessive disorders", "locations": [{"offset": 15530, "length": 29}]}, {"id": "21861", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D030342", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D030342"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D030342", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Genetic Diseases Inborn", "accession": "@DISEASE_Genetic_Diseases_Inborn"}, "text": "autosomal recessive disorders", "locations": [{"offset": 15601, "length": 29}]}, {"id": "21862", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 15848, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21863", "infons": {"identifier": "tmVar:rs74315294;VariantGroup:6;CorrespondingGene:1376;RS#:74315294;CorrespondingSpecies:9606", "type": "Variant", "valid": true, "subtype": "SNP", "database": "litvar", "gene_ids": [1376], "gene_id": 1376, "rsids": ["rs74315294"], "species_ids": [9606], "species_id": 9606, "rsid": "rs74315294", "normalized": ["rs74315294##", "#1376#"], "normalized_id": "rs74315294##", "biotype": "variant", "name": "rs74315294", "accession": "@VARIANT_p.S113L_CPT2_human"}, "text": "rs74315294", "locations": [{"offset": 15918, "length": 10}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 15965, "text": "Nonsynonymous or stop-gain mutations variants of uncertain significance were identified in all of the genes studied, except for FANCI and are summarized in Supplementary table 2. These variants were unable to be classified as benign or pathogenic because the only evidence available for evaluating biological consequence of these mutations was in-silico predictions from computational programs and prevalence of the variant in the general population, which are not sufficient to classify variants definitively using ACMG criteria.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21864", "infons": {"identifier": "55215", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "49530", "valid": true, "normalized": [55215], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 55215, "biotype": "gene", "name": "FANCI", "accession": "@GENE_FANCI"}, "text": "FANCI", "locations": [{"offset": 16093, "length": 5}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 16497, "text": "Variants classified as likely benign (n = 33) were found in WRN (n = 18), ATM (n = 7), POLG (n = 4), GRN (n = 1), LDLR (n = 2), and SOD1 (n = 1). Thirty-two of these variants were associated with nonsynonymous mutations and one was associated with a stop-gain mutation (Supplementary table 2).", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21865", "infons": {"identifier": "472", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "30952", "valid": true, "normalized": [472], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 472, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ATM", "accession": "@GENE_ATM"}, "text": "ATM", "locations": [{"offset": 16571, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "21866", "infons": {"identifier": "5428", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2016", "valid": true, "normalized": [5428], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5428, "biotype": "gene", "name": "POLG", "accession": "@GENE_POLG"}, "text": "POLG", "locations": [{"offset": 16584, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21867", "infons": {"identifier": "2896", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "1577", "valid": true, "normalized": [2896], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 2896, "biotype": "gene", "name": "GRN", "accession": "@GENE_GRN"}, "text": "GRN", "locations": [{"offset": 16598, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "21868", "infons": {"identifier": "3949", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "55469", "valid": true, "normalized": [3949], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 3949, "biotype": "gene", "name": "LDLR", "accession": "@GENE_LDLR"}, "text": "LDLR", "locations": [{"offset": 16611, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21869", "infons": {"identifier": "6647", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "392", "valid": true, "normalized": [6647], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6647, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SOD1", "accession": "@GENE_SOD1"}, "text": "SOD1", "locations": [{"offset": 16629, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21870", "infons": {"identifier": "7486", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "6659", "valid": true, "normalized": [7486], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 7486, "biotype": "gene", "name": "WRN", "accession": "@GENE_WRN"}, "text": "WRN", "locations": [{"offset": 16557, "length": 3}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "title_1"}, "offset": 16820, "text": "Discussion", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 16831, "text": "We observed that variants previously classified as pathogenic in both autosomal dominant and autosomal recessive disorders were seen in similar or higher frequencies among individuals from long lived families as compared to the general population. This study sequenced seven (BRCA1, SDHC, TP53, LMNA, LDLR, PTEN, and SMAD3) of the 59 genes in the ACMG list of incidental findings. This is the first study to systematically evaluate the prevalence of pathogenic mutations in long lived families and tracked transmission of pathogenic mutations across 2 generations within families that demonstrate exceptional longevity. The results from this study is consistent with the finding from the previous study of 44 Ashkenazi Jewish centenarians; in both studies, the frequencies of pathogenic variants are not significantly different from those of the general population. In the Ashkenazi centenarian study, 130 coding variants in genes associated with degenerative, neoplastic and cardiac diseases classified as pathogenic or likely pathogenic were identified. Though participants in this study are younger than participants in centenarian studies, the results from this study are also consistent with previous studies on centenarians that showed that centenarians without phenotypic evidence of specific diseases have similar prevalence of variants associated with complex chronic diseases as the general population. In addition, the results from this study are also consistent with genomic sequencing performed in general risk populations that have shown that pathogenic mutations can be observed in individuals without any evidence of clinical disease. Furthermore, other studies have reported pathogenic mutations in BRCA1 in women without a family history of breast cancer and pathogenic mutations in SCN5A or KCNH2 in patients without phenotypic and electrophysiological evidence of cardiac arrhythmias. These findings suggest that established pathogenic variants may have incomplete penetrance in individuals without a strong family history of the specific disorder.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21872", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 17107, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21873", "infons": {"identifier": "6391", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2256", "valid": true, "normalized": [6391], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6391, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SDHC", "accession": "@GENE_SDHC"}, "text": "SDHC", "locations": [{"offset": 17114, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21874", "infons": {"identifier": "7157", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "460", "valid": true, "normalized": [7157], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 7157, "biotype": "gene", "name": "TP53", "accession": "@GENE_TP53"}, "text": "TP53", "locations": [{"offset": 17120, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21875", "infons": {"identifier": "4000", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "41321", "valid": true, "normalized": [4000], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 4000, "biotype": "gene", "name": "LMNA", "accession": "@GENE_LMNA"}, "text": "LMNA", "locations": [{"offset": 17126, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21876", "infons": {"identifier": "3949", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "55469", "valid": true, "normalized": [3949], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 3949, "biotype": "gene", "name": "LDLR", "accession": "@GENE_LDLR"}, "text": "LDLR", "locations": [{"offset": 17132, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21877", "infons": {"identifier": "5728", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "265", "valid": true, "normalized": [5728], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5728, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTEN", "accession": "@GENE_PTEN"}, "text": "PTEN", "locations": [{"offset": 17138, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21878", "infons": {"identifier": "4088", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "55937", "valid": true, "normalized": [4088], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 4088, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SMAD3", "accession": "@GENE_SMAD3"}, "text": "SMAD3", "locations": [{"offset": 17148, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21879", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 18547, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21880", "infons": {"identifier": "6331", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "22738", "valid": true, "normalized": [6331], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6331, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SCN5A", "accession": "@GENE_SCN5A"}, "text": "SCN5A", "locations": [{"offset": 18632, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21881", "infons": {"identifier": "3757", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "201", "valid": true, "normalized": [3757], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 3757, "biotype": "gene", "name": "KCNH2", "accession": "@GENE_KCNH2"}, "text": "KCNH2", "locations": [{"offset": 18641, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21882", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "breast cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 18590, "length": 13}]}, {"id": "21883", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001145", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001145"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001145", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Arrhythmias Cardiac", "accession": "@DISEASE_Arrhythmias_Cardiac"}, "text": "cardiac arrhythmias", "locations": [{"offset": 18715, "length": 19}]}, {"id": "21884", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "women", "locations": [{"offset": 18556, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21885", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D006331", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D006331"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D006331", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Heart Diseases", "accession": "@DISEASE_Heart_Diseases"}, "text": "cardiac diseases", "locations": [{"offset": 17807, "length": 16}]}, {"id": "21886", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D019636", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D019636"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D019636", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neurodegenerative Diseases", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neurodegenerative_Diseases"}, "text": "degenerative, neoplastic", "locations": [{"offset": 17778, "length": 24}]}, {"id": "21887", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002908", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002908"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002908", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Chronic Disease", "accession": "@DISEASE_Chronic_Disease"}, "text": "chronic diseases", "locations": [{"offset": 18200, "length": 16}]}, {"id": "21888", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D030342", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D030342"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D030342", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Genetic Diseases Inborn", "accession": "@DISEASE_Genetic_Diseases_Inborn"}, "text": "dominant and autosomal recessive disorders", "locations": [{"offset": 16911, "length": 42}]}, {"id": "21889", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 18650, "length": 8}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 18900, "text": "The ACMG list of reportable genes is associated with monogenic diseases that have an intervention available to prevent the disease or lessen its symptoms. However, a recent ACMG guideline on return of secondary genetic findings has clarified that the ACMG list of 59 genes recommended for reporting of incidental genetic findings was intended to be applied only in the context of clinical whole exome/genome sequencing and not intended to be applied for general population screening. Consistent with the ACMG position and results from previous studies, this study show at least two pathogenic variants in genes associated with autosomal dominant conditions, BRCA1 and SDHC, that did not result in overt disease in the LLFS participants. In addition, three LLFS participants were homozygous for the CPT2 variant, rs74315294, which is the most commonly identified mutation in people with CPT II deficiency that can be characterized by recurrent episodes of myalgia and weakness. These three LLFS participants also did not specifically report muscle weakness, although they were not adequately assessed for this particular phenotype. Despite the ACMG guidelines on return of secondary genetic findings, there is no clear consensus among healthcare professionals regarding return of incidental findings of pathogenic variants. Findings from this study and previous studies have significant implications for expanding large scale sequencing efforts to the general population without a strong family history of specific diseases.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21890", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 19558, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21891", "infons": {"identifier": "6391", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2256", "valid": true, "normalized": [6391], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6391, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SDHC", "accession": "@GENE_SDHC"}, "text": "SDHC", "locations": [{"offset": 19568, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21892", "infons": {"identifier": "1376", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "77", "valid": true, "normalized": [1376], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1376, "biotype": "gene", "name": "CPT2", "accession": "@GENE_CPT2"}, "text": "CPT2", "locations": [{"offset": 19698, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21893", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 19889, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21894", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C563462", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C563462"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C563462", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carnitine Palmitoyltransferase II Deficiency Infantile", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carnitine_Palmitoyltransferase_II_Deficiency_Infantile"}, "text": "CPT II deficiency", "locations": [{"offset": 19786, "length": 17}]}, {"id": "21895", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D063806", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D063806"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D063806", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Myalgia", "accession": "@DISEASE_Myalgia"}, "text": "myalgia", "locations": [{"offset": 19855, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "21896", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 19618, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21897", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D018908", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D018908"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D018908", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Muscle Weakness", "accession": "@DISEASE_Muscle_Weakness"}, "text": "weakness", "locations": [{"offset": 19867, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "21898", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D018908", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D018908"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D018908", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Muscle Weakness", "accession": "@DISEASE_Muscle_Weakness"}, "text": "muscle weakness", "locations": [{"offset": 19940, "length": 15}]}, {"id": "21899", "infons": {"identifier": "tmVar:rs74315294;VariantGroup:6;CorrespondingGene:1376;RS#:74315294;CorrespondingSpecies:9606", "type": "Variant", "valid": true, "subtype": "SNP", "database": "litvar", "gene_ids": [1376], "gene_id": 1376, "rsids": ["rs74315294"], "species_ids": [9606], "species_id": 9606, "rsid": "rs74315294", "normalized": ["rs74315294##", "#1376#"], "normalized_id": "rs74315294##", "biotype": "variant", "name": "rs74315294", "accession": "@VARIANT_p.S113L_CPT2_human"}, "text": "rs74315294", "locations": [{"offset": 19712, "length": 10}]}, {"id": "21900", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 19656, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21901", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D004194", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D004194"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D004194", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Disease", "accession": "@DISEASE_Disease"}, "text": "monogenic diseases", "locations": [{"offset": 18953, "length": 18}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 20424, "text": "This study has several strengths and limitations. Compared to other studies on long lived individuals, the large sample size and the generalizability of the study findings to people of broad European descent are significant strengths of this study, though these findings may not be generalizable to individuals of non-European ancestry. Furthermore, since several LLFS participants with pathogenic mutations were relatively young, the diseases associated with the autosomal dominant diseases might not have manifested yet. For example, the participants with the BRCA1 variant were in their sixties, which is still relatively young in terms of clinical manifestation of genetic breast or ovarian cancer. A previous study has shown that though the peak incidence of breast cancer was among women in their 40s and 50s, the cumulative risk of breast and ovarian cancer risk increased till 80 years. Thus, these LLFS participants could develop breast or ovarian cancer in the future. Follow-up of LLFS participants over ~ 8 years showed that the 92 year old father with the BRCA1 mutation and the 99 year old mother with the SDHC mutation died of non-cancer related causes while the remaining LLFS participants are alive and have not reported any new diagnosis of cancer during the intervening years. The lack of any family history of autosomal dominant diseases in these families suggests that the pathogenic mutations may not be fully penetrant in these individuals and is these results lend further support to the recent clarification of the ACMG guidelines on reporting secondary genetic findings in the context of general population screening efforts. Despite the large sample size, the low population prevalence of these variants may limit estimation of differences in population prevalence for some variants in LLFS as compared to general population based databases. For example, this study had only 78% power (alpha = 0.05) to detect differences in population frequency for the BRCA1 variant (frequency = 0.03%), while this study had 87% power (alpha = 0.05) to detect differences in population frequency for the SDHC variant (frequency = 0.08%). Future studies that extend these results beyond the 25 genes to all 59 genes listed in the ACMG secondary findings list in other large, more diverse long-lived populations and extending our results will further clarify the penetrance of pathogenic mutations in populations without a strong family history of specific diseases.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21902", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 20986, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21903", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 21493, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21904", "infons": {"identifier": "6391", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2256", "valid": true, "normalized": [6391], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6391, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SDHC", "accession": "@GENE_SDHC"}, "text": "SDHC", "locations": [{"offset": 21544, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21905", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA1", "locations": [{"offset": 22405, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21906", "infons": {"identifier": "6391", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2256", "valid": true, "normalized": [6391], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 6391, "biotype": "gene", "name": "SDHC", "accession": "@GENE_SDHC"}, "text": "SDHC", "locations": [{"offset": 22540, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21907", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 21612, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21908", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 20788, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21909", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D061325", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D061325"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D061325", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Hereditary_Breast_and_Ovarian_Cancer_Syndrome"}, "text": "breast or ovarian cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 21363, "length": 24}]}, {"id": "21910", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D030342", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D030342"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D030342", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Genetic Diseases Inborn", "accession": "@DISEASE_Genetic_Diseases_Inborn"}, "text": "autosomal dominant diseases", "locations": [{"offset": 21754, "length": 27}]}, {"id": "21911", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 21416, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21912", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D061325", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D061325"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D061325", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Hereditary_Breast_and_Ovarian_Cancer_Syndrome"}, "text": "breast and ovarian cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 21263, "length": 25}]}, {"id": "21913", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 22237, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21914", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 21570, "length": 6}]}, {"id": "21915", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 21683, "length": 6}]}, {"id": "21916", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D000094024", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D000094024"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D000094024", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Post-Acute COVID-19 Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Post_Acute_COVID_19_Syndrome"}, "text": "LLFS", "locations": [{"offset": 21331, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "21917", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "women", "locations": [{"offset": 21212, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "21918", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D030342", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D030342"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D030342", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Genetic Diseases Inborn", "accession": "@DISEASE_Genetic_Diseases_Inborn"}, "text": "autosomal dominant diseases", "locations": [{"offset": 20888, "length": 27}]}, {"id": "21919", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D061325", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D061325"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D061325", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Hereditary_Breast_and_Ovarian_Cancer_Syndrome"}, "text": "breast or ovarian cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 21101, "length": 24}]}, {"id": "21920", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "breast cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 21188, "length": 13}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "CONCL", "type": "title_1"}, "offset": 22921, "text": "Conclusions", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "CONCL", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 22933, "text": "The study results suggest that penetrance of pathogenic variants may be lower in a general population as compared to targeted patient populations with a strong family history of specific Mendelian diseases. The lack of overt disease in two generations of family members with pathogenic mutations in this study further supports the idea that populations without a strong family history of specific conditions may demonstrate incomplete penetrance of pathogenic variants. These findings suggest that family history of specific diseases should be an important consideration in deciding whether specific incidental genetic findings should be returned to research participants to minimize potential harm while maximizing patient benefit. Hence, before expanding large scale genomic testing to asymptomatic individuals in the broader community, additional research is needed to better understand genotype-phenotype associations and penetrance of genetic variants in the general population.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21921", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patient", "locations": [{"offset": 23059, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "21922", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patient", "locations": [{"offset": 23649, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "21923", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D030342", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D030342"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D030342", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Genetic Diseases Inborn", "accession": "@DISEASE_Genetic_Diseases_Inborn"}, "text": "Mendelian diseases", "locations": [{"offset": 23120, "length": 18}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "SUPPL", "type": "title_1"}, "offset": 23917, "text": "Supplementary information", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "ABBR", "type": "title"}, "offset": 23943, "text": "Abbreviations", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "ABBR", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 23957, "text": "ACMG", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "21924", "infons": {"type": "Disease", "valid": false, "normalized_id": null, "biotype": "disease"}, "text": "ACMG", "locations": [{"offset": 23957, "length": 4}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "ABBR", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 23962, "text": "American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "r